    // Battle 33 is a close fight under the matrix's spawn jitter (Q0041, Q0044). With the
    // zealot's StarCraft II weapon (damage point 0, every 21 ticks, range 0.1, backswing 9;
    // plan 2026-11-04-combat-sc2-alignment WP4), the marine's (damage point 1, backswing 13;
    // WP6; speed 0.126 per tick, WP7), StarCraft II firing arcs (WP17 commit d: both fire within
    // 11.25 degrees of their facing), hull turning (WP17 commit f: both turn 55.99 degrees per
    // tick, where they turned instantly), a swing that starts on the tick its turn aligns it
    // (plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP1, M-22) and StarCraft II's keep-target rule (WP4,
    // B-9: a unit whose target is out of weapon reach takes the closest candidate, so a chasing
    // zealot no longer follows its first marine while another is up to 1.0 closer), on 68 seeds
    // (the four of record plus 64 jittered ones, jitter 0.12) the marines win 20, the zealots
    // win 35 and 13 are unresolved at 500 ticks; marine survivors average 1.85 (SD 2.46, range 0
    // to 8), zealot survivors 1.76 (SD 1.52, range 0 to 5). Before B-9 it was 37 / 20 / 11
    // (3.62), before WP1 39 / 20 / 9 (3.87), after the arcs 43 / 16 / 9 (4.38), before WP17
    // 42 / 18 / 8 (4.03), after combat alignment WP4 alone 30 / 24 / 14 (3.09), and before that
    // WP4 a marine win on 61 of the 68 (7.41). The expectation is the smallest ranges that hold
    // on all 20 matrix seeds since B-9 (orchestrator, plan Amendment 5; the seeds of record are
    // 0-2, 3-0, 0-2 and 2-1, marines - zealots left); a seed outside them is re-recorded by the
    // commit that causes it. What varies is how many zealots reach the marines at once.
    // Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes.md §4.6 (B-9) and §1 (WP1), and
    // docs/evidence/2026-11-04-combat-sc2-alignment.md §14.7 (§14.4 for the arcs, §6, §5 and §3
    // for WP7, WP6 and WP4, and §1 for the earlier figures, from
    // docs/evidence/2026-11-03-battle-33-investigation.md §4.2).
    (
